W: 1. Will you go to the rolling of the stones
W: The tossing of the ball?
W: Or will you go and see pretty Annie
W: Dancing among them all?
W:
W: 2. Will you drink of the blood
W: The white wine and the red
W: Or will you go and see pretty Annie
W: Dancing among the dead.
W:
W: 3. I will not go to the rolling of the stones
W: Or the tossing of the ball
W: But I will go and see pretty Annie
W: Dancing among them all.
W:
W: 4. They had not danced a single dance
W: Nor tapped the hall around
W: When a knife that had come from his brother's side
W: Gave him a deadly wound.
W:
W: 5. They picked him up and carried him along
W: They layed him down on the ground
W: And there he laid till the break of day
W: And made not a single sound.
W:
W: 6. Annie's come awandering by
W: A tablet all under her arms
W: She went till she came to her true love's grave
W: And there she began to charm.
W:
W: 7. She's charmed the fish out of the sea
W: The birds out of their nests
W: She's charmed her true love out his grave
W: Till he could no longer rest.
W:
W: 8. Will you go to the rolling of the stones
W: The tossing of the ball?
W: Or will you go and see pretty Annie
W: Dancing among them all.
